    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d631">

                <pb facs="0672" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8884: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-08T16:00:00+02:00">March 8, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>888. The Embassy hears from a fairly reliable source that Gesandter Schwörbel,
                    Chief of the Southwestern [<hi rendition="#italic">Southeastern</hi>] European
                    Section of the German Foreign Office,<anchor n="42a" xml:id="d631-f1"/> is
                    either en route to or has arrived at Athens for the purpose of promoting a Greek
                    compromise settlement with Italy.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Athens.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d631-f1" n="42a" xml:id="d631-f1-content">
                <p>Paul Schwörbel, head of the Division for Southeast Europe and the Near East in
                    the News Service and Press Department of the German Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
